WEBVTT

00:15.563 --> 00:17.940
JOJO'S BIZARRE ADVENTURE
DIAMOND IS UNBREAKABLE

00:19.233 --> 00:22.527
<i>These faceless gazes pass by one another</i>

00:22.903 --> 00:26.197
<i>A wound to the heart changes our everyday</i>

00:26.407 --> 00:30.907
<i>Encounters without boundaries
The bizarre is our normal U-yeh</i>

00:33.414 --> 00:36.708
<i>These ordinary mornings,
we're laughing on the surface</i>

00:36.792 --> 00:40.420
<i>Mysteries drawn to each other,
identity still unknown</i>

00:40.504 --> 00:45.004
<i>Without a heads up,
it's quietly lurking somewhere in this town</i>

00:49.597 --> 00:54.097
<i>Although we bicker and complain
In the end, we celebrate</i>

00:56.645 --> 01:00.023
<i>Dancing through the everyday</i>

01:00.107 --> 01:04.607
<i>Crazy Noisy Bizarre Town</i>

01:16.624 --> 01:20.753
EPISODE 13
WE PICKED UP SOMETHING CRAZY!

01:17.124 --> 01:19.167
<i>Welcome to Morioh Radio,</i>

01:19.251 --> 01:20.774
<i>Where today we hear from
"Languishing Lonesome Boy."</i>

01:23.756 --> 01:25.174
<i>"Kai, hear me out," he writes.</i>

01:25.633 --> 01:28.886
<i>"My girlfriend just ghosted me,
and I'm super depressed"</i>

01:28.969 --> 01:32.847
<i>"I think I may've scared her off
with my out-of-the-blue proposal."</i>

01:33.015 --> 01:36.852
<i>"And I spent my whole paycheck on
her birthstone engagement ring…"</i>

01:43.192 --> 01:45.819
So you've safely recovered
the bow and arrow.

01:46.070 --> 01:48.614
Yeah, I found it
in Akira Otoishi's apartment.

01:49.031 --> 01:51.742
He'd been using his Stand
to help himself to a few things.

01:52.159 --> 01:54.035
A few things worth 500 million yen.

01:54.328 --> 01:56.747
Police are already on it.

01:57.623 --> 01:59.708
<i>Go ahead and try
using your Stand again.</i>

02:00.042 --> 02:02.377
<i>I'll hunt you down,
and wipe you off the face of the earth.</i>

02:04.004 --> 02:06.131
<i>You can't get me in here!</i>

02:06.715 --> 02:08.550
Chili Pepper's spent.

02:08.801 --> 02:12.054
Even if he were to break loose,
I don't think he'd try anything.

02:14.974 --> 02:17.518
Mr. Jotaro, what about
the bow and arrow?

02:18.018 --> 02:20.520
It'll go to the Speedwagon Foundation
for analysis.

02:20.855 --> 02:24.233
It'll help us unravel
the mystery of Stands.

02:24.400 --> 02:25.484
Great!

02:25.651 --> 02:26.943
Hallelujah!

02:27.319 --> 02:29.446
Then that solves it!

02:29.780 --> 02:32.991
That seemed almost too easy,
but hooray! We did it!

02:33.117 --> 02:35.994
We're still interrogating Otoishi

02:36.203 --> 02:38.205
about the other Stand users
this thing unleashed.

02:39.039 --> 02:40.457
So stay on your toes, just in case.

02:40.749 --> 02:41.499
- Yeah.
- Right.

02:43.002 --> 02:46.088
The Japanese sure
do know their coffee.

02:46.380 --> 02:48.590
Waitress, refill please!

02:48.757 --> 02:51.092
Watch ou—! Christ…

02:51.302 --> 02:52.720
You have to pay attention!

02:53.095 --> 02:55.055
I look away and…

02:58.100 --> 03:00.894
Josuke, isn't it time?
The bus'll be here soon.

03:02.146 --> 03:04.731
Oh… yeah…

03:05.441 --> 03:06.650
Guess you're right.

03:07.276 --> 03:10.529
Come on, let's go. Upsy daisy.

03:15.576 --> 03:17.578
I wonder about those two.

03:17.786 --> 03:19.454
I'm worried.

03:20.206 --> 03:23.876
Whoa, this cake is top notch!

03:24.168 --> 03:25.794
Waitress, more cake!

03:33.969 --> 03:38.098
- Higashikata residence, this is—
<i>- Oh, Mom. It's me.</i>

03:38.849 --> 03:39.724
Josuke?

03:40.226 --> 03:42.394
That's a surprise. You never call.

03:42.853 --> 03:44.145
Well, what is it?

03:44.605 --> 03:49.105
Well, uh… Y-You're going
to be home all day, right?

03:50.110 --> 03:52.737
Yeah? What's this about?

03:52.947 --> 03:55.199
N-Nothing!
As long as you'll be there. Bye!

03:55.449 --> 03:56.366
Hey!

03:56.784 --> 03:57.826
What in the…?

03:58.118 --> 04:01.496
He'd better not be up to something.

04:01.747 --> 04:02.748
Shit…

04:03.123 --> 04:07.168
I hope Mom hasn't caught on
to any of this…

04:08.837 --> 04:10.296
For Pete's sake…

04:10.464 --> 04:13.341
I said wait until I'm off the phone!

04:21.392 --> 04:22.851
Um, one sec!

04:24.061 --> 04:27.189
Hello? Can you hear me? Hey!

04:28.565 --> 04:31.484
Now, did you just call for me?

04:31.610 --> 04:34.446
Yeah. We'll never get
a taxi at this hour.

04:34.697 --> 04:36.865
We're taking the bus to my house.

04:37.116 --> 04:38.700
All right, here it goes…

04:39.243 --> 04:41.995
I know I sound pushy,
but I'll say it again.

04:43.455 --> 04:45.331
Make sure you keep your distance.

04:45.499 --> 04:49.211
And no talking to Mom!

04:49.503 --> 04:50.587
Promise me.

04:51.380 --> 04:55.217
Paying her a visit won't
be enough to make her happy.

04:55.884 --> 04:58.052
She'll be beside herself.

05:00.681 --> 05:05.060
I know that. And I promise.

05:05.311 --> 05:07.438
One more thing.

05:07.688 --> 05:11.775
I'm gonna be calling you
Mr. Joestar.

05:12.067 --> 05:13.026
Huh?

05:13.444 --> 05:17.406
W-Well, I might as well
come right out and say it.

05:17.698 --> 05:20.409
Well, someone I've just met…

05:21.076 --> 05:22.243
I know this sounds harsh…

05:22.536 --> 05:27.036
calling that person
"Dad" or "Father" just isn't me.

05:29.918 --> 05:31.461
Once you see Mom,

05:31.545 --> 05:33.880
I'd appreciate it if you'd make
a beeline back to America.

05:36.383 --> 05:38.259
Right…

05:38.552 --> 05:41.596
Of course. I understand.

05:42.389 --> 05:46.101
<i>Crap, this couldn't be
anymore awkward.</i>

05:46.226 --> 05:48.394
<i>I know I should open up,</i>

05:48.520 --> 05:51.189
<i>but sometimes you just can't
push what isn't meant to be.</i>

05:54.401 --> 05:56.111
Hey, Mr. Joestar…

06:00.949 --> 06:04.744
Um, you didn't happen to see
a hulking, grandpa-looking fellow, did you?

06:05.079 --> 06:07.122
He just got on that long-haul bus.

06:08.707 --> 06:10.542
BRIGHT DEER
LONG DISTANCE BUS
TO SAPPORO

06:09.708 --> 06:10.563
Wh-What were you thinking? Dammit!

06:13.837 --> 06:15.630
Sorry about that.

06:15.714 --> 06:18.425
You said we were getting
on a bus, so…

06:18.675 --> 06:21.302
But you caught up to
the bus pretty well there.

06:21.512 --> 06:24.640
Looks like we were just
about to get on the freeway.

06:24.807 --> 06:28.727
I'm starting to think
I should've let you go…

06:28.811 --> 06:29.895
straight to Hokkaido!

06:30.771 --> 06:31.688
Ugh, damn cramp.

06:31.772 --> 06:33.899
Sorry about that.

06:39.029 --> 06:40.864
Josuke…

06:40.989 --> 06:44.617
I think something's pulling at my pants.

06:44.701 --> 06:48.830
Oh, yeah? Careful,
or it'll drag you off somewhere else.

06:49.790 --> 06:50.916
Wha…

06:57.172 --> 07:01.009
J-Josuke! A Stand user!

07:03.720 --> 07:07.014
Yeah, yeah.
Two in fact… you and I.

07:07.307 --> 07:10.935
Anywho, where's a vending machine
when you need it? I'm parched.

07:18.444 --> 07:22.156
<i>W-What the…?
These aren't footsteps.</i>

07:22.531 --> 07:24.866
<i>Hands? Handprints?</i>

07:31.582 --> 07:36.003
Oh my God!
Josuke, the Stand just laughed!

07:36.211 --> 07:38.588
Look! Right here! In the sand!

07:39.756 --> 07:43.468
<i>No way I can let him meet Mom.</i>

07:43.760 --> 07:45.636
<i>He's seeing and hearing things.</i>

07:46.346 --> 07:48.723
Damn, concrete!

07:48.807 --> 07:51.309
Where'd it go? Where is it?
It's gone!

07:51.393 --> 07:54.562
Where'd you go? You're gone!

07:55.481 --> 07:58.734
<i>Great. This old man is
nothing but trouble.</i>

08:06.617 --> 08:09.077
Hermit Purple!

08:18.170 --> 08:20.589
Beat it, mutt! Get! Get!

08:22.382 --> 08:25.176
Do you hear that crying?

08:26.094 --> 08:27.804
Over here, Josuke.

08:29.431 --> 08:33.351
It's a baby!
I have a naked baby in my hands.

08:33.852 --> 08:36.896
I can feel it. It's invisible!

08:36.980 --> 08:38.064
What?!

08:45.697 --> 08:46.864
I-It's there!

08:47.157 --> 08:48.491
It's really there!

08:48.617 --> 08:49.618
It's soft like a baby.

08:50.244 --> 08:52.287
I don't believe it…

08:52.454 --> 08:54.622
An invisible baby!

08:54.873 --> 08:58.167
It can't be more than
six months old or so.

08:58.377 --> 09:02.214
But how'd a baby turn invisible,
and out here?

09:02.589 --> 09:04.716
I'm guessing
it's the work of a Stand, but…

09:05.425 --> 09:08.928
Why would an enemy
Stand user turn a baby invisible?

09:09.221 --> 09:10.680
And where's its mother?

09:10.931 --> 09:12.974
It just doesn't add up.

09:14.851 --> 09:19.351
Josuke, I think the baby
is the Stand user.

09:20.482 --> 09:22.859
It just doesn't know it.

09:23.277 --> 09:25.821
It must have instinctively
turned itself invisible

09:25.904 --> 09:28.406
when it was separated from its mother.

09:28.490 --> 09:29.240
Huh?

09:29.408 --> 09:33.908
In adults, psychological
duress can trigger ulcers,

09:34.288 --> 09:38.750
hair loss, and hair greying.

09:39.042 --> 09:42.712
By finding its mother,
I think we might just be able to solve this.

09:43.880 --> 09:47.466
H-Hey, that's great,
just make it stop crying!

09:47.593 --> 09:49.845
I-I don't know what to do, either.

09:49.970 --> 09:54.015
I have some experience,
but that was a very long time ago.

09:54.182 --> 09:56.350
There, there…

09:57.644 --> 09:58.686
Th-This is…

10:00.063 --> 10:01.355
Did you figure it out?

10:01.565 --> 10:04.276
Yes, I could tell by touch.

10:08.155 --> 10:09.865
It's a girl.

10:09.990 --> 10:14.035
Oh right, it's what's
between the legs that counts!

10:17.664 --> 10:19.499
Something else I should know about?

10:20.167 --> 10:21.418
Josuke,

10:22.419 --> 10:23.878
do you have any tissues?

10:28.467 --> 10:30.010
Th-That smell…

10:30.177 --> 10:34.222
I-Is it in your hand? A big one?

10:34.848 --> 10:38.518
I had no idea until I got a noseful!

10:38.644 --> 10:41.605
I just scratched my beard
with this hand!

10:48.779 --> 10:51.573
JOSUKE HIGASHIKATA

10:54.242 --> 10:56.494
Here is your manuscript back.

10:56.828 --> 11:00.456
I'm looking forward to
those revisions, Sensei.

11:02.918 --> 11:07.297
For now, I guess we'll need
to pick up formula and diapers.

11:07.381 --> 11:10.801
And since she's going au naturale,
we need to get her some clothes.

11:13.387 --> 11:15.430
I'm counting on you, Mr. Joestar.

11:15.555 --> 11:18.057
What? I-I'm buying them?

11:18.183 --> 11:22.187
Of course!
You forget what I look like?

11:22.270 --> 11:25.273
I can't go in there
and buy baby stuff.

11:25.482 --> 11:26.941
People will start to talk.

11:27.192 --> 11:31.362
That I'm some 16-year-old bad boy
who knocked up some poor chick.

11:32.072 --> 11:36.572
But I only have
American traveler's checks.

11:37.202 --> 11:38.912
All right…

11:39.329 --> 11:41.622
Put it on my card.

11:41.790 --> 11:43.291
Sorry…

11:43.875 --> 11:46.127
Now stay away
from the expensive stuff.

11:46.420 --> 11:49.464
I've worked hard to
build up that little nest egg!

11:49.589 --> 11:51.966
Of course, of course.

11:52.592 --> 11:53.926
Welcome.

11:54.302 --> 11:56.595
Can I help you find something?

11:56.763 --> 11:59.766
Um, have any disposable
diapers lying around anywhere?

11:59.933 --> 12:02.602
We do carry those!
Your first time?

12:04.104 --> 12:06.981
Yes, I suppose it is…

12:07.607 --> 12:09.150
These diapers are a cinch to change,

12:09.234 --> 12:12.195
even for customers
living without assistance.

12:12.112 --> 12:13.696
SUPER ABSORBENT
ADULT DIAPERS

12:12.279 --> 12:13.697
You'll rest well with these.

12:15.866 --> 12:19.661
Um… they're not for me,
they're for a baby.

12:19.995 --> 12:22.163
Oh, goodness gracious,
how rude of me!

12:22.581 --> 12:25.250
Of course they're for a baby!

12:26.501 --> 12:30.505
Will we be needing traditional
diapers or training pants today?

12:30.881 --> 12:32.591
Uh… What was that?

12:32.883 --> 12:36.511
As you can see, although
traditional diapers require a cover,

12:36.636 --> 12:39.847
they're more economical and
less wasteful than training pants.

12:40.390 --> 12:44.394
I-I'm not really sure, could you just…

12:44.686 --> 12:46.145
And what about the size?

12:46.646 --> 12:47.688
Size?

12:48.148 --> 12:49.816
May I ask how old is the baby?

12:50.025 --> 12:51.401
Depending on
your child's unique shape,

12:51.485 --> 12:55.985
we have preemies, small, medium, large,
and extra large for both boys and girls.

12:59.117 --> 13:02.245
My, how things have changed…

13:02.704 --> 13:05.373
W-Well, she's a girl,

13:05.457 --> 13:08.042
and when I held her,
she was about this big.

13:08.168 --> 13:10.795
When you held her?
I'm afraid I don't follow.

13:11.046 --> 13:14.716
Unfortunately, if you were
to return ill-fitting soiled diapers,

13:14.800 --> 13:17.052
you would be putting us in
a difficult situation.

13:17.177 --> 13:21.431
Um, understood.
Then I'll take every size you have.

13:21.681 --> 13:25.226
I also need baby wipes,
instant formula, and baby bottles…

13:25.560 --> 13:29.063
We carry both glass
and plastic baby bottles.

13:29.147 --> 13:29.689
Huh?

13:29.773 --> 13:32.358
Glass bottles tend to
be scratch and odor resistant,

13:32.442 --> 13:34.902
but can be heavy for a baby to hold.

13:34.986 --> 13:38.739
Plastic bottles may be light,
but they are not odor free.

13:38.949 --> 13:40.617
Which would you like?

13:40.951 --> 13:45.451
U-U-Uh… Um…

13:45.997 --> 13:48.457
We carry all sorts of
shapes and designs.

13:48.625 --> 13:51.252
We have rocket ships and racing cars.

13:51.378 --> 13:53.421
This one, the baby can hold by itself.

13:53.547 --> 13:58.047
And when you turn this one upside down,
the doll does a delightful little dance.

13:58.385 --> 14:02.885
I-I really don't know,
so just pick a few and…

14:03.014 --> 14:05.016
And what about bottle nipples?

14:05.141 --> 14:08.602
Rubber ones are soft,
but lack in durability.

14:08.770 --> 14:12.356
Silicon nipples are resilient,
but tend to be rigid.

14:12.566 --> 14:14.859
This is our "Choopa Trainer."

14:14.943 --> 14:16.819
A diaphragm valve in the nipple,

14:16.903 --> 14:19.155
coupled with the baby's own
suckling pressure

14:19.239 --> 14:22.492
function to regulate the flow of milk.

14:22.576 --> 14:24.452
This is the made-in-Germany brand Nuk.

14:24.536 --> 14:26.496
Moderately compressed into an oval,

14:26.746 --> 14:29.165
the nipple is designed to
mimic the mother's natural shape.

14:29.374 --> 14:31.334
And just like with mother,

14:31.418 --> 14:34.587
milk will not flow
without the baby's jaw movement.

14:34.754 --> 14:38.048
O-Oh, that'll do.
Whatever you think.

14:38.133 --> 14:39.592
I'll take them all then.

14:39.676 --> 14:43.471
We also carry circular-, Y-, and
cross-shaped varieties of nipple openings.

14:45.932 --> 14:47.850
J-Just give me all of them.

14:47.934 --> 14:51.395
And I'll need some
baby clothes and socks, too.

14:55.400 --> 14:57.985
Oh, and I'd like to pay by card.

14:58.278 --> 14:59.779
Thank you very much.

15:01.698 --> 15:06.198
130,000…
Now what might the exchange rate be.

15:06.912 --> 15:09.331
In dollars that would come to…

15:09.414 --> 15:12.667
If 100 yen is about 80 cents…

15:14.628 --> 15:16.004
Well, in any case.

15:16.129 --> 15:19.841
It's all for a good cause,
and it's just baby stuff.

15:19.966 --> 15:22.885
How expensive could it be?

15:23.803 --> 15:25.304
Goddammit..

15:25.639 --> 15:28.266
What's he doing?
He's taking forever.

15:28.350 --> 15:29.184
By the way…

15:29.309 --> 15:31.978
The girl who got the ring.
What happened with that?

15:32.145 --> 15:34.397
Does no reply mean "no"?

15:34.606 --> 15:37.900
- She's probably just conflicted.
<i>- I can't take it anymore…</i>

15:38.234 --> 15:41.195
<i>If someone from class
sees me here…</i>

15:41.529 --> 15:43.822
Sorry 'bout that, Josuke.

15:44.074 --> 15:45.575
Here's your card.

15:45.825 --> 15:48.327
All done?
Okay, great, chop chop.

15:54.292 --> 15:57.503
Now we won't have to
worry about losing her, but…

15:57.837 --> 16:01.423
Without a face, she'll freak out
anyone who looks at her.

16:01.675 --> 16:03.176
I've already thought of that…

16:03.718 --> 16:06.053
I picked up some makeup, too.

16:06.471 --> 16:09.098
First, a little foundation…

16:09.182 --> 16:10.558
There and there…

16:15.939 --> 16:19.192
You know, she's actually kinda cute.

16:19.442 --> 16:21.235
Beautiful, beautiful!

16:21.444 --> 16:24.864
This will help us find her mom.

16:25.156 --> 16:28.409
Now we're getting somewhere.
We can do this!

16:28.702 --> 16:30.120
Good thinking!

16:30.370 --> 16:34.870
That's what I like to hear!
Now for the lipstick.

16:35.458 --> 16:37.626
Now a few strokes for
the eyebrows and eyelashes…

16:37.711 --> 16:39.045
A little here, a little there…

16:41.381 --> 16:43.508
<i>Why am I not surprised..</i>

16:43.675 --> 16:46.886
<i>A little flattery and
this old man's walking on air.</i>

16:47.053 --> 16:50.890
Now walking around the neighborhood
with you will be a piece of cake.

16:51.349 --> 16:55.019
And since we can't powder your eyes,
sunglasses should do the trick.

16:56.312 --> 16:57.771
It's just perfect!

16:58.481 --> 16:59.648
Here's some milk.

17:02.110 --> 17:04.612
Maybe I went too light
on the foundation.

17:04.696 --> 17:07.407
It doesn't look like it's sticking…

17:10.869 --> 17:11.953
Th-That's not it!

17:12.037 --> 17:14.372
What the hell?! Sh-She's…

17:16.624 --> 17:19.293
Sh-She's gone! My hands!

17:19.586 --> 17:22.297
Her own body isn't the only thing
she's making invisible!

17:22.422 --> 17:24.924
She's doing the same
to her surroundings!

17:26.134 --> 17:28.010
Mr. Joestar! Let go of the baby!

17:28.094 --> 17:31.388
I said let go of the damn baby!

17:33.433 --> 17:36.102
I-I let go,
but they're still invisible!

17:36.269 --> 17:37.395
She's powering up!

17:53.953 --> 17:55.454
This isn't good.

17:56.081 --> 17:58.458
Everything within
a thirty-centimeter radius

17:58.583 --> 18:01.294
has gone completely invisible!

18:01.920 --> 18:04.172
But it doesn't make sense.

18:04.547 --> 18:06.882
She can't be trying to
protect herself with her Stand.

18:06.966 --> 18:10.552
Who could feed her or look after her?

18:10.929 --> 18:14.182
So the effect is anxiety-induced.

18:14.557 --> 18:16.058
It's stress.

18:16.559 --> 18:19.603
She doesn't like to be
handled by people she doesn't know.

18:19.813 --> 18:22.982
If she powers up any more,
no one will be able to get near her.

18:23.066 --> 18:25.068
We'll end up invisible, too.

18:27.987 --> 18:31.365
What a weird heap of junk.
Someone better pick that up.

18:31.825 --> 18:33.493
Well, someone will take care of it.

18:33.576 --> 18:35.077
Not gonna be me.

18:36.579 --> 18:38.038
Look out!

18:41.709 --> 18:42.960
What happened?

18:43.044 --> 18:46.797
This lit cigarette was…
Of course, you can't see it.

18:50.844 --> 18:53.054
What in the devil
are you doing, Mr. Joestar?!

18:53.930 --> 18:57.058
Get with it, man!

18:57.684 --> 19:00.812
I, uh…

19:06.526 --> 19:08.319
The stroller completely disappeared!

19:09.112 --> 19:10.571
And it took the ground with it!

19:10.697 --> 19:12.365
So it is stress!

19:12.532 --> 19:15.743
The greater her distress,
the more she makes invisible!

19:18.913 --> 19:21.206
I think I heard the stroller flipping over!

19:27.338 --> 19:31.258
The invisible baby…
fell into the water?!

19:32.051 --> 19:34.970
Wh-Where is she?
Make some noise!

19:35.096 --> 19:37.223
I don't see any bubbles!
Where is she?!

19:37.432 --> 19:39.267
J-Josuke…

19:39.350 --> 19:40.309
Shut the hell up!

19:41.936 --> 19:44.855
<i>We're in this mess
because of this shuffling fool.</i>

19:45.148 --> 19:46.941
<i>Old senile has-been!</i>

19:47.066 --> 19:50.652
<i>This irresponsible jackass
is my father?</i>

19:50.904 --> 19:52.030
<i>A man so irresponsible,</i>

19:52.113 --> 19:54.281
<i>he had no problem discarding
my mom for sixteen years.</i>

19:54.741 --> 19:57.702
<i>No way I can respect
someone like him.</i>

19:57.952 --> 20:00.454
<i>There was no way
this was ever gonna work out.</i>

20:01.915 --> 20:02.665
You…

20:02.916 --> 20:04.167
Stay out of this!

20:08.922 --> 20:11.424
<i>Where is she?
She's gotta be around here somewhere…</i>

20:11.966 --> 20:14.009
<i>I don't care if I turn invisible, too.</i>

20:14.302 --> 20:16.846
<i>Just touch me! Hurry!</i>

20:16.971 --> 20:18.347
<i>Come on!</i>

20:19.933 --> 20:21.851
<i>She's no there… Hurry!</i>

20:23.436 --> 20:26.647
<i>Shit!
How do I find a transparent baby</i>

20:26.773 --> 20:29.150
<i>in transparent water?!</i>

20:30.777 --> 20:33.738
Josuke, I…

20:34.113 --> 20:37.658
won't be able to
hold on much longer, so…

20:37.951 --> 20:42.451
tell your mother
hello for me, would ya?

20:43.957 --> 20:45.375
After all…

20:46.209 --> 20:48.878
I am just an old man, you know.

20:52.215 --> 20:53.841
What the hell are you doing?!

20:55.218 --> 20:59.513
I'm giving it some color…

21:05.311 --> 21:07.146
The center…

21:07.480 --> 21:10.900
The blood disappears
toward the middle.

21:11.109 --> 21:15.279
In the center… the child…

21:18.116 --> 21:19.867
Mr. Joestar…

21:28.084 --> 21:31.587
No ordinary person
would dream up such a thing.

21:31.671 --> 21:34.256
Not for a strange child.
Not for someone else's child…

21:34.924 --> 21:36.133
This is…

21:42.056 --> 21:44.892
I was trying to look cool…

21:45.018 --> 21:46.728
for you.

21:54.277 --> 21:56.946
HERMIT PURPLE

22:01.534 --> 22:04.119
Well, that was an experience…

22:04.412 --> 22:07.456
All's well that ends well, I guess.

22:14.547 --> 22:17.091
O-One hundred and thirty thousand yen?!

22:17.216 --> 22:20.052
All my hard-earned money…

22:20.178 --> 22:24.098
- You rotten old man…!
- There, there.

23:39.090 --> 23:42.009
EPISODE 14
LET'S GO TO
THE MANGA ARTIST'S HOUSE, PART 1
